# Backend Rules (FastAPI)

## Layout

Work under `backend/app/` and `backend/worker/`:

- `api/v1` — routers
- `services` — app-facing logic
- `db/repositories` — persistence
- `providers` — X / News / Reddit / Official adapters
- `pipeline` — intelligence processing
- `domain` / `schemas` — domain + API DTOs

## Router rules

MUST: validate input, call services, return schemas.  
MUST NOT: business logic, direct DB/session queries, provider/LLM calls.

## Service rules

MUST: personalization, brief assembly, signal reads.  
MUST NOT: FastAPI types, raw SQL, external HTTP to sources.

## Worker rules

Ingest and analyze run in `worker/`, not in request handlers.
Persist Events first; publish Signals only after quality gate + daily quota.

## Evidence integrity

- Community-only sources (X/Reddit) must NOT become `confirmed_fact` without trusted corroboration.
- Separate fact / interpretation / opinion / rumor explicitly.

## Schemas

Use Pydantic response models. Do not expose SQLAlchemy models directly from routers.

## Config

Use `app.core.config.Settings`. Tesla MVP knobs: `daily_signal_cap`, min importance/confidence, RSS URL.

## Logging

Log ingest/process counts and gate rejections. Never log secrets or full PII.
